# Optional. Unset (the default) is correct for local dev — Vite's dev
# server proxies /api/* to the Express server (see vite.config.ts), so
# relative fetch('/api/...') calls just work with no config here.
#
# In a split production deployment (this client on Vercel, the API on
# Render — see docs/DEPLOY.md), there's no such proxy: client and server
# are different origins. Set this to the deployed API's exact URL, no
# trailing slash, e.g.:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL="https://pathway-api.onrender.com"
#
# This is read at BUILD time (Vite inlines import.meta.env.VITE_* at
# build, not at runtime) — set it as a Vercel project environment
# variable, not in a .env file that ships with the deploy.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
